.TH GIT-PS 1 2026-09-24 git-workflow "git-workflow manual"
.SH NAME
git-ps \- sync with the remote branch, then push
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git ps
.RB [ force ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rebase the current branch onto its remote copy (if there is one), then
.BR "git push \-u" .
Pushing a protected branch warns first, or stops when
.B workflow.strict
is true.
.PP
If the branch was rewritten after it was pushed (by
.BR git\-sq (1),
a rebase or an amend),
.B git ps
stops and says to use
.BR "git ps force" ,
instead of replaying the old commits on top of the rewritten ones.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR force ", " \-f
Push with
.B \-\-force\-with\-lease \-\-force\-if\-includes
and no sync. The remote is overwritten only if its tip is something this
branch has already seen, so commits that only arrived through a
background fetch are never lost. Protected branches are never
force-pushed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-sq (1),
.BR git\-workflow (7)
